From 978d784581efd36b294bd0d20dc7a3b9d7acb4bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:32:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ship libbrotli's licence alongside brotlicffi's own

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every brotlicffi wheel on PyPI, so this needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

The extension statically links the bundled libbrotli C sources
(libbrotli/c, compiled as the "libbrotli" static library by setup.py), which
carry their own MIT notice from the Brotli Authors. Those terms require the
copyright notice to travel with binary redistributions, but setup.cfg's
explicit license_files list names only brotlicffi's LICENSE, so the built
wheel ships a single notice covering the wrapper alone.

Naming the vendored file in place keeps the patch to one line and lets it
track the submodule: setuptools preserves each license_files entry's path
relative to the project root, so it lands in the wheel as
dist-info/licenses/libbrotli/LICENSE.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.cfg | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index 8b7eaaf..d3d94fa 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -6,3 +6,4 @@ markers =
 [metadata]
 license_files =
     LICENSE
+    libbrotli/LICENSE
